<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        Acquisitions gap-fix, Item 1A (2026-08-30, agent-output/design-requirements.md §2
        ITEM 1). Requires Rejection_Reason__c to be populated on the save that a deal ARRIVES
        at Dead/Pass. The picklist value is literally 'Dead/Pass' - stored as Dead%2FPass in
        picklist/BusinessProcess/RecordType metadata only, never at formula runtime. TEXT() is
        used on Rejection_Reason__c only to normalize a blank picklist to an empty string for
        ISBLANK(); StageName is compared with ISPICKVAL(), matching this org's own
        Specific-Function-Guideline that ISPICKVAL() is required for picklist equality.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 AMENDED 2026-08-30 (same day, later decision): INSERT-TIME ENFORCEMENT ADDED.
        =====================================================================================
        The rule originally gated on ISCHANGED(StageName) alone, so a deal created directly AT
        Dead/Pass (never having been at any other stage) escaped it entirely - ISCHANGED() is
        always false on insert. The user decided this is a real gap, not an accepted one: a
        deal created straight into Dead/Pass with no reason must be blocked too. The gate is
        now OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(StageName)) - ISNEW() is a standard formula function
        supported in validation rules at this API version (67.0), returning TRUE only on the
        record's very first save.

        🔴 THE OBVIOUS SIMPLER FIX WAS CONSIDERED AND REJECTED: dropping ISCHANGED() entirely
        to leave AND(ISPICKVAL(StageName,'Dead/Pass'), ISBLANK(TEXT(Rejection_Reason__c)))
        would fire on EVERY SUBSEQUENT SAVE of an already-Dead/Pass record that has no reason -
        making every historical reasonless Dead/Pass deal permanently uneditable, including the
        9 rows scripts/seed-pipeline.apex creates (that script has been updated separately, by
        the developer agent, to set Rejection_Reason__c at insert so it stays green under the
        NEW insert-time gate - but records seeded before this rule existed, or by any other
        historical process, must NOT be locked out of ordinary edits by this rule).

        THREE CASES, STATED SO A FUTURE EDIT CAN SELF-CHECK AGAINST THEM. Do not "tighten" this
        formula without re-verifying all three:
          - INSERT at Dead/Pass, reason blank                              -> BLOCK (new)
          - UPDATE moving INTO Dead/Pass, reason blank                     -> BLOCK (unchanged)
          - UPDATE of a record ALREADY AT Dead/Pass, reason blank, stage
            UNCHANGED                                                     -> ALLOW, DELIBERATELY.
        The third case is the one a "tightening" edit is most likely to break by mistake (e.g.
        by simplifying OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(StageName)) down to something that fires on every
        save regardless of transition). It is allowed ON PURPOSE so every historical
        already-Dead/Pass record without a reason stays editable for unrelated field changes -
        the rule's job is to gate the ARRIVAL at Dead/Pass, not to retroactively police records
        that arrived there before this rule (or its insert-time amendment) existed.

        WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE RULE FROM No_Backward_Stage_Movement, NOT A CLAUSE ADDED TO IT:
        the two rules need different errorDisplayFields (this one points at
        Rejection_Reason__c; No_Backward_Stage_Movement points at StageName) and different
        error messages. Folding this logic into that rule's single errorConditionFormula would
        force one generic message to serve two unrelated failure reasons. See also
        Dead_Pass_Not_Allowed_From_Closed_Won.validationRule-meta.xml, which is the OTHER new
        rule in this same tranche and is NOT related to this one beyond sharing the object.
    -->
    <fullName>Rejection_Reason_Required_On_Dead</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Requires a Rejection Reason when a deal ARRIVES at Dead/Pass - on insert or a stage change into it. Does not fire on a later save of a record already at Dead/Pass, stage unchanged, so historical reasonless records stay editable. See the XML comment.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    OR(ISNEW(), ISCHANGED(StageName)),
    ISPICKVAL(StageName, &apos;Dead/Pass&apos;),
    ISBLANK(TEXT(Rejection_Reason__c))
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>Rejection_Reason__c</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>Choose a Rejection Reason when a deal is set to Dead/Pass.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
